# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored by Vite's defaults) and edit.
# Every key must be prefixed VITE_ or Vite will not expose it to the client.

# Bypass authentication entirely: no Authorization header, no token refresh, no
# sign-in redirect, every route open. Set this when pointing the console at the
# standalone tcketmanage-app, which serves core's endpoints without an auth stack
# and has no /api/auth for the sign-in page to call.
#
# Development builds only. `src/lib/devAuth.js` ANDs this with import.meta.env.DEV,
# which Vite replaces at build time, so a production bundle drops the bypass as
# dead code regardless of what this is set to. A fixed badge sits in the bottom-left
# of every page while it is on, so you cannot forget.
#
# VITE_DISABLE_AUTH=true
